Advanced turbulent statistics, spectra and energy-budget study (@fd-advanced-statistics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Turbulence-McDonough.lingua#r_2TBK3JC1KJ1CMNABRW3Y2AFKTQ", #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA", #source "../sources/Johns-Hopkins-Turbulence-Databases.lingua#r_1D25T86CC1CHT4BX098WQXBQPE", #source "../sources/PIV-Uncertainty-Sciacchitano.lingua#r_4PHTCFRTAGSCNV1TK192VZHGQ6", #fluid-dynamics "Advanced-turbulence-closure-verification-and-validation-study.lingua#r_6S38T31W8P5CSNRDF9Y77KPYF7") { r_0460VC6BHC9TM4E3HRAS38M2XH
**Read:** [Introductory Lectures on Turbulence — James M. McDonough](../sources/Turbulence-McDonough.lingua#r_2TBK3JC1KJ1CMNABRW3Y2AFKTQ), complete statistical and scaling development; [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA), complete turbulence chapter; [Johns Hopkins Turbulence Databases — numerical flow evidence](../sources/Johns-Hopkins-Turbulence-Databases.lingua#r_1D25T86CC1CHT4BX098WQXBQPE), dataset methods and cited primary simulation; [Uncertainty quantification in particle image velocimetry — Sciacchitano](../sources/PIV-Uncertainty-Sciacchitano.lingua#r_4PHTCFRTAGSCNV1TK192VZHGQ6), uncertainty in measured statistics.

Use a fully documented numerical turbulence dataset or physical time/space measurements to reconstruct means, Reynolds stresses, correlations, spectra and an appropriate energy budget. Preserve normalization, filtering, forcing, resolution and sampling choices. Reproduce one independently published statistic before asking a new question.

Test stationarity, record length, spatial sampling and effective independent sample count. Compare scale estimates and inertial-range hypotheses with the actual accessible range. Evaluate at least one third-order or transport relation where its assumptions apply, and identify the influence of anisotropy, inhomogeneity or finite Reynolds number.

Report sampling uncertainty and systematic limits separately. Explain how alternative estimators or observation filters change the result and which conclusions remain robust. For [Johns Hopkins Turbulence Databases — numerical flow evidence](../sources/Johns-Hopkins-Turbulence-Databases.lingua#r_1D25T86CC1CHT4BX098WQXBQPE), retain the selected simulation and access-method metadata; a publicly accessible DNS is numerical evidence with its own model and resolution limits, not a universal experimental ground truth.

**Continue:** [Advanced turbulence-closure verification and validation study](Advanced-turbulence-closure-verification-and-validation-study.lingua#r_6S38T31W8P5CSNRDF9Y77KPYF7).

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics — motion, forces, transport and evidence](../Fluid-dynamics.lingua#r_7PQW1WDHK708BFV23MD8ET61VZ).
